<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN>



<PLUGIN
  name="docktail-preview"
  author="vcolombo"
  version="2026.09.20"
  launch="Settings/DockTail"
  pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/main/plugin/docktail-preview.plg"
  support="https://github.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/issues"
  min="7.0.0"
>

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[

### 2026.09.20

## Changes

- Improve service enrollment and connection diagnostics, including inspection-failure reporting and Tailscale policy guidance.
- Read configuration as data rather than sourcing it as shell code, and explicitly report values that cannot be stored.
- Harden credential migration and file handling, reject stale settings saves, and serialize daemon lifecycle operations.
- Report start, stop, and restart failures instead of presenting misleading success messages.

## Updating

Update through Unraid **Plugins → Check for Updates**, then open **Settings → DockTail** and check configuration and service status. If the plugin reports refused or unreadable configuration, follow the displayed guidance before restarting.

The bundled DockTail version remains **1.7.9**.

Full changes: https://github.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/compare/2026.09.03.9.5...2026.09.20

### 2026.09.03.9.5

Labels tab layout fix.

The Enrolment table sat between the page heading and the builder, so on a server with a lot of containers the form you came for was pushed off screen - and the Label Builder heading had nothing visible under it. The builder now comes first and the Enrolment table sits at the end as reference.

### 2026.09.03.9.4

Licensing compliance for the packaged binary.

The package shipped DockTail's compiled binary without the AGPL-3.0 licence text or any pointer to its source. It now installs `LICENSE` and `SOURCE` alongside the binary in `/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail`, where `SOURCE` records the upstream repository, tag and exact commit the binary was built from.

No functional changes.


For older releases, see https://github.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/releases
]]>
</CHANGES>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/docktail/docktail-unraid-2026.09.20-noarch-1.txz">
<URL>https://github.com/vcolombo/docktail-unraid/releases/download/2026.09.20/docktail-unraid-2026.09.20-noarch-1.txz</URL>
<SHA256>e24b857c1165f794c3ec47cb17c405687088a3f6da6af5e78a6ca008bddee189</SHA256>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'install' script. Unraid re-installs every /boot/config/plugins/*.plg on
boot, so this runs at boot too: it must be idempotent and must not fail when
Docker or Tailscale are still down.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
if [ -d "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail" ]; then
    rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail
fi

mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/docktail

# Keep tailnet credentials out of Unraid Connect's flash backup, which is a git
# repo at /boot/.git. Both files' temps are listed, not just the credentials
# one: a save renames a staged file into place, a worker that dies between the
# two leaves that file behind, and the migration stages docktail.cfg from a
# state where it may still hold a credential it is about to move out.
#
# Before upgradepkg, not after: the package's doinst.sh runs the config
# migration, which stages those temps - so the patterns have to be on the flash
# before anything can write one.
printf 'credentials.cfg\ncredentials.cfg.tmp\ncredentials.cfg.tmp.*\ndocktail.cfg.tmp\ndocktail.cfg.tmp.*\n*.unreadable.*\n' > /boot/config/plugins/docktail/.gitignore

# Before upgradepkg, like the ignore file: the package's doinst.sh runs the
# migration, which records what the pair looked like - so the pair has to be
# complete before it looks, or the next boot reports a change that was just
# this install finishing.
#
# noclobber, not a test-then-create: an Apply can land between the two and this
# would then copy /dev/null over credentials it just saved. `set -C` makes the
# redirection itself fail when the file exists, which is one atomic syscall.
#
# The -e/-L test in front of it is not that race back again - `set -C` is still
# what guarantees nothing is overwritten. It is there because a redirection
# opens whatever is at the path, and opening a FIFO for writing blocks until
# something reads it: a named pipe left at credentials.cfg would hang this
# install, and it runs at boot. Testing first means a special file is never
# opened at all, and the branch below reports it instead.
if [ ! -e /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg ] && [ ! -L /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg ]; then
    (
        umask 077
        set -C
        : > /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg
    ) 2> /dev/null || true
fi

# Only a real file. chmod follows symlinks and has no option not to, so this
# line - running as root - would otherwise set 0600 on whatever a symlink left
# at that path happened to point at. The umask above already creates the file
# private, so this is for the one it did not create: an existing credentials
# file from a previous install, which the block above left alone.
if [ -f /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg ] && [ ! -L /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg ]; then
    chmod 0600 /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg
elif [ -e /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg ] || [ -L /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg ]; then
    echo "docktail: /boot/config/plugins/docktail/credentials.cfg is not a regular file - leaving it as it is. DockTail cannot store credentials there until it is replaced with one."
fi

upgradepkg --install-new /boot/config/plugins/docktail/docktail-unraid-2026.09.20-noarch-1.txz


# Drop the other release channel so both are never installed at once.
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/docktail.plg
rm -f /var/log/plugins/docktail.plg

# Start (or restart) the daemon. Deferred, so a blocking Unraid event returns
# immediately.
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail/restart.sh

# Clean up superseded packages.
rm -f $(ls /boot/config/plugins/docktail/docktail-unraid-*.txz 2>/dev/null | grep -v '2026.09.20')

echo ""
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo " docktail-preview has been installed."
echo " Plugin version:   2026.09.20"
echo " DockTail version: 1.7.9"
echo ""
echo " Configure it under Settings -> Network Services ->"
echo " DockTail. DockTail needs the Tailscale plugin and a"
echo " tagged Unraid node; the Status tab checks both."
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'remove' script. Settings under /boot/config/plugins/docktail are left in place:
Unraid convention is that plugin settings survive removal.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
/usr/local/etc/rc.d/rc.docktail stop 2>/dev/null

removepkg docktail-unraid

rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/docktail
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/docktail/*.txz
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
